<section class="lp-section">
    <div class="lp-head"><h2>Questions</h2></div>
    <div class="lp-faq">
        <details><summary>Who is WageHarbor for?</summary><p>US small businesses with salaried, hourly and contract (1099) workers who want to run payroll themselves, with clear pay stubs and self-service for their team.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does WageHarbor file my payroll taxes?</summary><p>No. WageHarbor calculates withholding and employer taxes and gives you the totals and reports (tax liability, Form 941 worksheet, W-2 and 1099 summaries). You or your accountant make the deposits and filings.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How do employees get paid?</summary><p>By direct deposit, using the ACH file WageHarbor creates for your bank, or by paper check.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can my bookkeeper or accountant use it?</summary><p>Yes. Give them a login with the Payroll or HR role, and they can run reports and export CSV files.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is my data safe?</summary><p>Sensitive numbers are encrypted, each company's data is kept separate, and access is based on roles. See <a href="security">Security</a> for details.</p></details>
    </div>
</section>

